2. **Real bug** — TestLoaderLegacy: the legacy flow (no subscription answered) *still contacted the registry* and failed. Because the template declares a message-ref parameter, `prepareCreateTemplate` fetches the export whenever the template has refs — even when the user wires topic/contract manually. The fetch happens before resolution to feed prompt suggestions, but a legacy flow without a reachable registry shouldn't fail.

   Design fix: the export fetch feeds (a) prompt suggestions and (b) post-resolution validation. If no message-ref field has a value after resolution, the export was only needed for suggestions. Failing the whole create because the suggestion source is down is wrong. Options:

   A. Fetch lazily: fetch before prompting; if it fails, degrade: no suggestions (note on stderr), continue; after resolution, if a message-ref field has a value → fetch again (or fail if unreachable then). Double-fetch complexity.

   B. Fetch once, tolerate failure: keep err; if after resolution some message-ref value exists and export==nil → return the fetch error; else proceed with note "message registry unavailable; no suggestions".

   B is cleaner: one fetch, tolerate when unused. Implement: fetchMessageRegistry returns (doc, err); in prepareCreateTemplate, keep fetchErr; proceed with prompter without suggestions (note to stderr: "message registry unreachable; message suggestions unavailable"); after ResolveWith: if any message-ref field has a non-empty value → if export nil → return fetchErr wrapped; else resolve. If no message-ref value → return nil subs.

